HST Office: print scaling in HST Sheets where people print (print dialog, Format menu, print preview).

"Fit all columns on one page" and the related choices were only in Format ▸ Page Style ▸ Page ▸ Scale. Now:
- Print dialog (File ▸ Print, General tab, under the copies): a "Scaling" list (vcl printdialog.ui "scalingbox"
  and its label "scalingboxlabel", hidden unless the application offers the list; vcl shows the label with the
  list). Calc offers it (ScPrintUIOptions, property "PrintScaling") with No Scaling (print sheets at their actual
  size), Fit Sheet on One Page, Fit All Columns on One Page, Fit All Rows on One Page, and "Custom Scaling: …" when
  the current sheet has another scaling (75 %, N pages, W × H pages). Opening the dialog changes nothing; once an
  entry is picked, the printed sheets get it before the pages are counted, so the dialog preview, the page count
  and the printout follow at once. The custom entry gives every printed sheet back what it had when the dialog
  opened. Not offered for a read-only or shared document.
- Commands .uno:PrintScaleNone, .uno:PrintScaleFitSheet, .uno:PrintScaleFitColumns, .uno:PrintScaleFitRows (radio
  state of the current sheet), .uno:PrintScaleOptions (the page style dialog on its Page tab, where the HST scale
  controls are) and the drop-down .uno:PrintScaleMenu (popupmenu/printscale.xml; ResourceMenuController and
  GenericPopupToolbarController). They work on the selected sheets in the normal view and on the shown sheet in the
  print preview; the menu is in Format (after Print Ranges) and on the print preview toolbar (before the scaling
  factor slider). The ribbon buttons are in hst-sheets-print-scaling-ribbon.patch.
- sc::printscale (sc/source/ui/docshell/printscale.cxx) maps the choices onto the page style items Calc already has:
  none = ATTR_PAGE_SCALE 100; sheet = ATTR_PAGE_SCALETO 1×1; columns = 1×0; rows = 0×1 (the other two items 0, as
  the page dialog writes them). 1×1 and 1×0 are what .xlsx stores as fitToPage with fitToWidth/fitToHeight, and
  what .ods stores as scale-to-X/Y, so the choice survives both formats; PDF export uses the page style as printing.
  Scaling belongs to a sheet, as in other spreadsheet programs: a sheet whose page style is shared with a sheet
  that does not get the same scaling first gets its own copy of the style ("PageStyle_<sheet name>", the name the
  spreadsheet import gives), so other sheets keep their printout. One undo step ("Change Scale") covers the style
  copy, its assignment and the change.
- Strings: sc strings.hrc (dialog entries, custom labels), vcl printdialog.ui, CalcCommands.xcu labels and tips;
  Vietnamese in sc/vcl messages.po and UI.po ("Thu phóng", "Vừa tất cả các cột trên một trang", …; dialog-opening
  labels without an ellipsis in Vietnamese).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files are MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/unit/test_sheets_print_scaling_patch.py; runtime: tests/runtime/check-sheets-print-scaling.py (page
counts of a wide sheet printed to PDF with each choice, undo, .xlsx and .ods round trip, print dialog list).
